resources.string:
"[Principle] Dilation is the dual of erosion: the set of all z such that the structuring element B translated by z has at least one point in common with set A; it expands the boundary outward and bridges small holes and cracks.
[Eq. 3-10] A ⊕ B = { z | [(B̂)_z ∩ A] ⊆ A }
[Eq. 3-11] A ⊕ B = { z | (B̂)_z ∩ A ≠ ∅ }
 The two formulas are equivalent; B̂ denotes the reflection of B (symmetric kernel).
[Parameters] Structuring element: 5×5 rectangle.
[Effect] The white foreground expands, holes shrink, and broken regions are connected."

"[Principle] Canny is the optimal edge-detection operator; the full pipeline has four steps:
[Eq. 4-34/4-35] ① Gaussian smoothing for denoising; ② Sobel computes the gradient magnitude and direction;
[Eq. 4-36/4-37] ③ Non-maximum suppression: keep only the local magnitude maxima along the gradient direction, thinning thick edges to single pixels;
[Eq. 4-38/4-39] ④ Hysteresis double-threshold detection and linking: above the high threshold T2 are strong edges, between T1~T2 are weak edges; a weak edge is kept only when connected to a strong edge.
[Parameters] T1 = 50, T2 = 150.
[Effect] The best edge map: continuous, thin and sharp edges with very little noise."
